            <div xml:id="d851">

                <pb facs="1047" n="937" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg937"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11358: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-02-04T16:00:00+08:00">February 4, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received February 4—1:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>12. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“February 14, 3 p.m. U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> fired
                            upon yesterday by field piece at mileage 117. Fire silenced with
                            twenty-two 3-inch shells and <pb facs="1048" n="938" xml:id="pg938"/>
                            1750 rounds machine gun. No casualties on <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Oahu</hi>. Steam launch <hi rendition="#italic">Mei Lu</hi>,
                            squadron’s [<hi rendition="#italic">Standard Oil Company?</hi>] vessel,
                            fired upon at mileage 204 and at Temple Hill yesterday. No
                            casualties.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Department.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
